/* book: lead: Loss sets how far a link reaches; rise time sets how fast it can run. Each part of the link slows the edges of a pulse, and a pulse that spreads too much runs into its neighbour. The rise-time budget adds these slowdowns and compares the total with the bit period. With the power budget it gives two maximum lengths, one set by attenuation and one by dispersion; the shorter is the real reach. */
