/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A rise time is the 10 % to 90 % time of a step response.
   - tsys is the system rise time; all four terms in the same unit (ns or ps).
   - With bit period Tb = 1/B, the rule is tsys ≤ 0.7Tb for NRZ and tsys ≤ 0.35Tb for RZ, whose pulse fills only half the slot.
   - The source width dominates.
   - Solving the power budget for L gives the attenuation limit Latt = (PT − PR − joint losses − M) ÷ α: with 28 dB available, no joints or margin and 0.22 dB/km, 127 km.
   - The dispersion limit is where the fiber term uses up the allowance: Ldisp = √((0.7/B)² − ttx² − trx²) ÷ (|D|σλ) for single-mode fiber.
   - The reach is the smaller of the two: loss wins at low bit rates, dispersion at high ones, crossing near 160 Mbit/s for the Fabry–Perot laser and 3.2 Gbit/s for the DFB.
*/
